  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is placed on a rough inclined plane. The inclination of the plane is gradually increased until the block just begins to slide down. The sin of angle made by the plane with horizontal is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math> when the block start sliding. The coefficient of friction between the block and the plane is (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)",
    "image": null
  },
